## Comparison with published figures

Our numbers are set against Clean Cities 2025, ECF QECIO v2.10, the BikeNetKit dataset and official city figures. Each external figure is stored with its source, its network scope, its length basis where known and its retrieval date [ADR 0001, ADR 0006, ADR 0008]. The comparison lists the gaps and explains them; it does not average them away. Clean Cities 2025 mostly used figures the cities submitted, and QECIO publishes results per NUTS3 region only. The rankings therefore differ in definition, denominator and boundary, not only in data.

## Berlin plan network overlay

The Berlin plan page sets our mapped km against the city's planned cycle network: the Senate's `radverkehrsnetz` WFS layer with its two classes, Vorrangnetz (priority network) and Ergänzungsnetz (supplementary network), in EPSG:25833 as served. For every Berlin LAU run of the report classifier, the cached OSM snapshot is read and classified again, and the recomputed tier totals must equal the stored run totals; no new OSM run is made [M8 spec, decision 10]. A way-side of tier A or B counts as on the network over the parts of it that lie within a buffer of a network line whose direction differs from its own by at most a maximum angle; parts shorter than a minimum length are dropped. The parameters are data. A parameter change is a new overlay version, and the rows of earlier versions stay in the database [M8 spec, decision 11]. The page shows the latest version.

